# Laravel — Project Conventions

This is the **Laravel 13** backend in the Tripteki parallel-codebase family. It is a **modular monolith** (REST only) and shares one REST contract and the same event names and payloads with FastAPI and NestJS. Nuxt and Next can use any of the three backends. The product brand is **Codebase**.

## Family conventions

| Topic | Rule |
|-------|------|
| Roles | Exactly `superadmin`, `admin`, `user` through `RoleEnum` |
| Brand | `APP_NAME` Codebase. Primary `#2563eb`, secondary `#84cc16`, tertiary `#1e3a8a` |
| Locales | `en`, `id`, `ms` under `lang/` and `src/{Module}/lang/` |
| GraphQL | Not used. REST only |
| Tenancy | `IS_TENANCY=false` keeps the shared contract. `true` enables the Laravel-only `/{tenant}` routes and the `Event` module |
| Realtime | Laravel Reverb + Echo on private channel `user.{id}` (FastAPI and Nest use Socket.IO rooms `user:{id}`) |
| Rate limit | Production only (`Throttle::middleware()` returns no limiter outside production) |
| Format | Indent 4, double quotes, trailing commas, no space before `(` (Pint `laravel` preset, `pint.json`) |
| Docs | Keep PHPDoc. Class names are fully qualified with a leading `\` |
| Principles | SOLID, dependency injection, tight cohesion and loose coupling |
| Patterns | Repository, Spatie Data DTO, middleware, observer (events and listeners) |

## Stack

| Layer | Choice |
|-------|--------|
| Framework | Laravel 13 + PHP 8.3 (`.php-version` pins `8.3.13`) |
| Server | **Laravel Octane** (`composer dev`, `composer start`) |
| Architecture | Modular monolith via `nwidart/laravel-modules` |
| Auth | `tymon/jwt-auth` — `ACCESS_TOKEN` / `REFRESH_TOKEN` scopes |
| DTOs | Spatie Laravel Data |
| Permissions | Spatie Permission + `Gate::before` for superadmin |
| Query | Spatie Query Builder (filtering, sorting) |
| Activity log | Spatie Activitylog |
| Excel | maatwebsite/excel (import/export) |
| Broadcast | Laravel Reverb + Echo (private channels) |
| Mail | Blade templates in `src/Auth/resources/views/emails/` |
| Web Push | Optional VAPID |
| Queue/Cache | Redis in production, `sync` locally |
| Database | MySQL or PostgreSQL. SQLite for local runs and in-memory tests |

## Directory layout

```
app/                            # Application shell
  Helpers/                      # UrlHelper, BrandingHelper, SettingHelper, …
  Http/Middleware/
  Http/Responses/               # ApiErrorResponse, ApiValidationResponse
  Providers/
  Support/                      # QueryParser, Throttle, AdminSpreadsheetSupport, …
bootstrap/app.php               # Middleware, broadcasting, exception rendering
config/
routes/
  api.php                       # /version, /status
  channels.php                  # user.{id} private channel
  console.php                   # Scheduler (user:clean)
src/                            # Domain modules
  Auth/                         # JWT, signed links, mail templates
  User/                         # Profile, admin, settings, import/export, Web Push
  Acl/                          # Roles and permissions
  Notification/                 # Inbox, admin, broadcast
  Log/                          # Activity log, admin refresh broadcast
  Event/                        # Laravel-only tenancy module
  I18N/                         # Locale middleware
database/seeders/
lang/                           # Root translations (en, id, ms)
tests/                          # Shared test helpers
```

### Per-module structure

```
src/{Module}/
  app/
    Http/Controllers/
    Services/
    Repositories/
    Dtos/
    Events/
    Listeners/
    Jobs/
    Imports/                    # Excel import classes
    Exports/                    # Excel export classes
    Mail/
  routes/                       # Module route definitions
  Database/
    Migrations/
    Seeders/
  resources/views/
  lang/{en,id,ms}/
  composer.json                 # Module-specific dependencies
```

## Naming conventions

| Artifact | Convention | Example |
|----------|-----------|---------|
| Controller | PascalCase + Controller | `UserAdminController` |
| Service | PascalCase + Service | `UserAdminService` |
| Repository | PascalCase + Repository | `UserAdminRepository` |
| Validator DTO | PascalCase + Dto | `UserDto`, `UserUpdateDto` |
| Transformer DTO | PascalCase + TransformerDto | `UserTransformerDto` |
| Event | PascalCase past tense | `UserAdminExported` |
| Namespace | `Modules\{Module}\App\{Layer}` | `Modules\User\App\Http\Controllers` |

## Shared API contract (all backends)

### Endpoints
- REST base: `/api/v1`
- Swagger docs: `/api/docs` (PHP 8 attributes `#[OA\Get(...)]`)
- GraphQL is not used
- Health/status: `/api/status`

### Auth
- `POST /api/v1/auth/login` returns HTTP 201 `{ accessToken, refreshToken, accessTokenTtl, refreshTokenTtl }`
- Login body is `{ identifierKey, identifierValue, password, remember }`; `identifierKey` is `email` or `name` (optional, inferred from `@`)
- `PUT/PATCH /api/v1/auth/refresh`, `POST /api/v1/auth/register`, `POST /api/v1/auth/logout`
- Profile is `GET` and `PUT /api/v1/users/me`
- Signed pages on the frontend are `/auth/reset-password/{email}` and `/auth/verify-email/{email}`
- Echo authorizes private channels with `POST /broadcasting/auth` and the access token

### Error responses
```json
// Validation (HTTP 422), same detail shape and sentences as FastAPI
{ "detail": [{ "type": "string_too_short", "loc": ["body", "password"], "msg": "String should have at least 8 characters", "input": "123", "ctx": { "min_length": 8 } }] }

// Other errors (ApiErrorResponse)
{ "detail": "User not found" }
```

### Pagination
```json
{ "total": 0, "totalPage": 1, "perPage": 10, "currentPage": 1, "nextPage": null, "previousPage": null, "firstPage": 1, "lastPage": 1, "data": [] }
```

Query: `limitPage` (default 10, max 100), `currentPage`, `orders=field:asc|field:desc`, `filters=key:value,key:value`.

### Realtime
- Events: `v1.notification.created`, `v1.admin.refresh`, `v1.user.admin.{imported,imported-failed,exported,exported-failed,activated,deactivated}`, `v1.acl.{role,permission}.admin.{imported,imported-failed,exported,exported-failed}`
- Payload keys match FastAPI and Nest. Export `fileUrl` is `storage/export/{filename}`

### Rate limiting
- Named limiters: `api-read` (10/min), `api-write` (30/min), `api-refresh`, `api-register`
- Applied in **production only**

## Auth & ACL

- `Gate::before` grants all policies to central `superadmin`
- Permission checks on admin routes through policies
- Default superuser: `superuser@{APP_EMAIL_SERVER}` / `12345678`

## Environment variables

```
APP_NAME, APP_KEY, APP_URL, APP_ENV, APP_DEBUG, APP_LOCALE, APP_TIMEZONE, APP_EMAIL_SERVER
IS_TENANCY
FRONTEND_URL, CORS_ORIGIN
JWT_SECRET
OCTANE_HOST, OCTANE_PORT
DB_CONNECTION, DB_HOST, DB_PORT, DB_DATABASE, DB_USERNAME, DB_PASSWORD
MM_CLIENT, MM_HOST, MM_PORT, MM_PASSWORD    # Redis
QUEUE_CONNECTION
MAIL_DRIVER, MAIL_LOG_CHANNEL, MAIL_ADMIN_ADDRESS, MAIL_ADMIN_NAME
BROADCAST_CONNECTION=log|reverb
REVERB_APP_ID, REVERB_APP_KEY, REVERB_APP_SECRET, REVERB_HOST, REVERB_PORT, REVERB_SCHEME
VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY, VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY, VAPID_SUBJECT
FILESYSTEM_DISK
```

`CORS_ORIGIN` accepts a JSON array or a comma list, like FastAPI and Nest. `FRONTEND_URL` is used when it is empty.

## Setup commands

```bash
composer install
php artisan key:generate
php artisan jwt:secret
php artisan migrate
php artisan db:seed             # Roles, permissions, settings, superuser
php artisan storage:link
composer dev                    # Octane with --watch
```

## Required processes

Octane alone is not enough in production. Run these too:

```bash
php artisan reverb:start            # WebSocket server
php artisan queue:work --queue=user-admin-queue,acl-admin-queue,event-admin-queue,notifications,default
php artisan schedule:work           # user:clean every minute
```

## Testing

```bash
composer test     # PHPUnit Feature suite (SQLite in memory)
```

- `phpunit.xml` sets `DB_CONNECTION=sqlite`, `DB_DATABASE=:memory:`, `IS_TENANCY=true`, `QUEUE_CONNECTION=sync`, `MAIL_DRIVER=log`
- Helpers: `AuthenticatesWithJwt`, `InteractsWithAdminApi`, `InteractsWithTenancy` in `tests/`
- Call `loginToken()` before each authenticated request (logout blacklists the JWT)
- Default test user: `superuser@{APP_EMAIL_SERVER}` / `12345678` (`superuser@mail.com` when `APP_EMAIL_SERVER=mail.com`)

## Lint

```bash
composer lint         # Laravel Pint
composer lint:check   # Pint dry run
```
